title: Revert with a reason on caller-facing precompile errors

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The System and Storage builtins, the XCM precompile and the vesting precompile now return
    `Error::Revert` for failures the caller can act on. They used to return `Error::Error`, which
    traps with empty return data. Running out of gas while charging still traps.

    `pallet_revive::precompiles` adds `ensure_not_delegate_call`, `ensure_not_read_only`,
    `DELEGATE_CALL_DENIED` and `STATIC_CALL_DENIED`. `Error::try_to_revert` now also turns
    `RootNotAllowed`, `EcdsaRecoveryFailed` and `DispatchError::Token` into reverts.

    If you maintain a precompile, replace hand-written guards with the helpers. A `?` on a
    `DispatchError` still traps, so map pallet errors at the call site.

    ```rust
    // before
    frame_support::ensure!(
        !env.is_delegate_call(),
        pallet_revive::Error::<T>::PrecompileDelegateDenied,
    );
    if env.is_read_only() {
        return Err(pallet_revive::Error::<T>::StateChangeDenied.into());
    }

    // after
    ensure_not_delegate_call::<T>(env)?;
    ensure_not_read_only::<T>(env)?;
    ```

    Runtimes need no change and no storage migration.

- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    These calls used to fail with empty return data. They now revert with `Error(string)`, so
    `catch Error(string)` runs and `eth_call` shows the reason:

    - XCM or vesting called with `DELEGATECALL`:
      "illegal to call this pre-compile via delegate call".
    - XCM `send` / `execute`, vesting `vest` / `vestOther` / `vestedTransfer`, System `terminate`
      or Storage `clearStorage` / `takeStorage` called from a static call:
      "cannot modify state in a static call".
    - System `ownCodeHash` or any vesting call with the root origin: "root origin is not allowed".
    - System `ecdsaToEthAddress` with an invalid key: "invalid compressed public key".
    - System `terminate` with no contract to destroy: "no contract to terminate". A token error
      from its balance transfer reverts with that error's reason.
    - Storage `takeStorage` when the write fails, matching `clearStorage`.

    XCM `send` and `execute` now name the `pallet_xcm` error instead of a fixed sentence, for
    example "XCM execute failed: local execution incomplete at instruction 3:
    FailedToTransactAsset". Vesting calls name the `pallet_vesting` error instead of printing the
    `DispatchError` debug output.

    Out of gas still fails with empty return data. Update callers that check for empty return
    data or match the old XCM and vesting strings.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-xcm-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-vesting-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
